{
  "decision": "NO_CHANGE",
  "workflow_yaml": null,
  "rationale": "The workflow already implements the two evidence-supported optimizations that fit it: P-LIT-CANCEL-STALE is present via `concurrency` with `cancel-in-progress: true`, and P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT is present via `timeout-minutes: 360`. Other candidate patterns do not apply or are unsafe here: the Bazel patterns (P-LIT-BAZEL-PARALLEL/INCREMENTAL/DEPS) require a Bazel build, but this is a CodeQL workflow using build-mode `none` with no Bazel; P-LIT-GHA-CACHE offers only modest benefit and there is no active dependency installation to cache (Maven build is commented out, build-mode is `none`); P-LIT-FAIL-FAST (`fail-fast: true`) is contraindicated because each CodeQL language matrix outcome is typically a required check and cancelling siblings would lose coverage; P-LIT-CHANGE-FILTER/P-LIT-SELECT/P-LIT-BUILD-SELECT risk skipping required CodeQL status checks since any source change can affect analysis results. The CI history is explicitly `not_a_measured_baseline`, so P-LIT-HISTORY-TIMEOUT cannot be justified. No minimal, coverage-preserving change is supported.",
  "evidence_ids": ["P-LIT-CANCEL-STALE", "P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT", "P-LIT-FAIL-FAST", "P-LIT-GHA-CACHE", "P-LIT-BAZEL-INCREMENTAL", "P-LIT-BAZEL-DEPS", "P-LIT-CHANGE-FILTER", "P-LIT-HISTORY-TIMEOUT"]
}
